  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Complete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{144}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1$ in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,$\n$y=7\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t$",
  "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\sqrt{144}=12$ and $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=12\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.\n$$",
